{
    // ACT 1 Selection

    "699a84bf8e2052342f79b912 name": "Power Supply Run",
    "699a84bf8e2052342f79b912 description": "Power isn’t decided at the switch.\n\nIt’s decided long before that, by what reaches the right hands and what never does.\n\nAt the moment, the parts moving through those routes aren’t moving for me.\n\nYou’re going to correct that.\n\nFind the components, stage them at the weather station, and leave the area quiet.\n\nNo spectacle. No disruption.",
    "699a84bf8e2052342f79b912 startedMessageText": "Get the components in place. Keep the route clean.",
    "699a84bf8e2052342f79b912 successMessageText": "Good. Supply reached the point it needed to.",
    "699a84bf8e2052342f79b912 completePlayerMessage": "Components staged. Route is live.",
    "699a84bf8e2052342f79b912 declinePlayerMessage": "",
    "699a84bf8e2052342f79b912 failMessageText": "The route broke before it mattered. That can’t happen again.",
    "699a84bf8e2052342f79b912 note": "Locate and stage electrical components to establish a functioning route.",

    "22c12c8303c9175e1e48ccd5": "Locate 2 working Power Cords",
    "79d461113c226b89847d826e": "Place the Power Cords at the Woods weather station",
    "79ece080f5288aecf7be9bb7": "Locate 4 working Capacitors",
    "52ba51088792a479f6ed8f75": "Place the Capacitors at the Woods weather station",
    "e42d9afccf2965724c6e0979": "Locate 2 Spark Plugs",
    "6c7bb0aa4b37df4f65ff21b4": "Place the Spark Plugs at the Woods weather station",
    "13d20c8c736986e68349c5ef": "Locate 2 intact Car Batteries",
    "691bb31461aa07529d9012bb": "Place the Car Batteries at the Woods weather station",

    "6848f1776be936dd22573866 name": "Big Mags Wanted",
    "6848f1776be936dd22573866 description": "People like to think fights are decided by skill.\n\nUsually they’re decided by endurance.\n\nBy who keeps shooting after the other side can’t.\n\nRight now, the group I’m watching has too much staying power.\n\nYou’re going to tilt that balance.\n\nGet the magazines where they need to be and walk away before anyone notices they were ever yours.\n\nThat’s enough.",
    "6848f1776be936dd22573866 startedMessageText": "Get the magazines there and leave nothing behind but the result.",
    "6848f1776be936dd22573866 successMessageText": "Good. That changes the next engagement before it even starts.",
    "6848f1776be936dd22573866 completePlayerMessage": "Magazines placed. No one interfered.",
    "6848f1776be936dd22573866 declinePlayerMessage": "",
    "6848f1776be936dd22573866 failMessageText": "That placement mattered more than you think. Missing it has consequences.",
    "6848f1776be936dd22573866 note": "Acquire and place high-capacity magazines to shift future combat odds.",

    "520ba9d22db01c3f7b0c3cee": "Locate a 60-round STANAG magazine",
    "6d3f59f5774c02bccbd9c545": "Place the STANAG magazine in Customs storage building 11",
    "ccf627e3c6cd943cc568d156": "Locate a 60-round AK magazine",
    "4b29eb8074def08839e3e5c4": "Place the AK magazine in Customs storage building 11",
    "eda35066db1293a1e39cef81": "Locate a SureFire 60-round magazine",
    "94f36d90e5f2b7ff7007683f": "Place the SureFire magazine in Customs storage building 11",

    "684edc10a8af5086d3e6557b name": "Pressure Relief",
    "684edc10a8af5086d3e6557b description": "Anyone can function when the environment is easy.\n\nLight, distance, clear lines — all of that forgives hesitation.\n\nFactory at night doesn’t.\n\nIt strips everything down to instinct, timing, and nerve.\n\nThat’s where real control shows itself.\n\nGo there in the dark and prove you can work without comfort.\n\nNo wavering.",
    "684edc10a8af5086d3e6557b startedMessageText": "Night raid. Factory. No hesitation.",
    "684edc10a8af5086d3e6557b successMessageText": "Good. You stayed effective when most people start second-guessing themselves.",
    "684edc10a8af5086d3e6557b completePlayerMessage": "Targets dropped. Control never slipped.",
    "684edc10a8af5086d3e6557b declinePlayerMessage": "",
    "684edc10a8af5086d3e6557b failMessageText": "The dark only punishes uncertainty. You gave it room to.",
    "684edc10a8af5086d3e6557b note": "Eliminate PMCs during Factory night raids to demonstrate control under pressure.",

    "8dab0b7bbea3c6716f43fdb6": "Eliminate PMCs on Factory during night raids",

    // ACT 2 Observation

    "69ea1001b4c7a13f5a001001 name": "Surface Contracts",
    "69ea1001b4c7a13f5a001001 description": "Skier prefers noise around his business.\n\nSmall trades. Ordinary goods. Enough clutter to keep the real structure from standing out.\n\nThat only works on people who never look twice.\n\nYou’re going to look properly.\n\nFind the records tied to his movement, pull them cleanly, and send the data through.\n\nI don’t need disruption.\n\nI need shape.",
    "69ea1001b4c7a13f5a001001 startedMessageText": "Find the records. Don’t disturb the route.",
    "69ea1001b4c7a13f5a001001 successMessageText": "There it is. Hidden in plain sight, just like I expected.",
    "69ea1001b4c7a13f5a001001 completePlayerMessage": "Routing records secured and sent.",
    "69ea1001b4c7a13f5a001001 declinePlayerMessage": "",
    "69ea1001b4c7a13f5a001001 failMessageText": "You came back with fragments, not clarity. That leaves too much unresolved.",
    "69ea1001b4c7a13f5a001001 note": "Locate and extract routing records to reveal underlying trade structure.",

    "69ea1001b4c7a13f5a101001": "Locate Skier’s routing records at the Customs train depot office",
    "69ea1001b4c7a13f5a101002": "Secure the routing records",
    "69ea1001b4c7a13f5a101003": "Transfer the routing data",

    "69ea1002b4c7a13f5a001002 name": "Supply Discipline",
    "69ea1002b4c7a13f5a001002 description": "Prapor doesn’t improvise.\n\nHe repeats what works until repetition becomes habit, and habit becomes the system.\n\nThat makes him dependable.\n\nIt also makes him readable.\n\nGet me the records that show how his supplies cycle through Reserve.\n\nOnce I can see the pattern, I won’t need him to explain anything.",
    "69ea1002b4c7a13f5a001002 startedMessageText": "Pull the records and look for the routine inside them.",
    "69ea1002b4c7a13f5a001002 successMessageText": "Predictable. He’s more rigid than he realizes.",
    "69ea1002b4c7a13f5a001002 completePlayerMessage": "Supply records secured and transferred.",
    "69ea1002b4c7a13f5a001002 declinePlayerMessage": "",
    "69ea1002b4c7a13f5a001002 failMessageText": "If the cycle isn’t clear, the whole read loses value.",
    "69ea1002b4c7a13f5a001002 note": "Locate and extract supply records to identify repeated movement cycles.",

    "69ea1002b4c7a13f5a102001": "Locate Prapor’s supply records in the Reserve bunker command room",
    "69ea1002b4c7a13f5a102002": "Secure the supply records",
    "69ea1002b4c7a13f5a102003": "Transfer the supply data",

    "69ea1003b4c7a13f5a001003 name": "Soft Channels",
    "69ea1003b4c7a13f5a001003 description": "Not everything important moves as weapons or money.\n\nSome networks survive because people depend on them.\n\nThat dependence keeps them quiet, and quiet systems get ignored.\n\nThat’s useful.\n\nGet me the records that show where her support runs actually go.\n\nOnce the flow is visible, the weak points are too.",
    "69ea1003b4c7a13f5a001003 startedMessageText": "Track the records and leave the network untouched.",
    "69ea1003b4c7a13f5a001003 successMessageText": "Good. Quiet systems still leave pressure behind.",
    "69ea1003b4c7a13f5a001003 completePlayerMessage": "Distribution records secured and transferred.",
    "69ea1003b4c7a13f5a001003 declinePlayerMessage": "",
    "69ea1003b4c7a13f5a001003 failMessageText": "Without the full flow, all you have is guesswork.",
    "69ea1003b4c7a13f5a001003 note": "Locate and extract support records to map hidden distribution flow.",

    "69ea1003b4c7a13f5a103001": "Locate Therapist’s distribution records in the Pharm 2 back office on Streets",
    "69ea1003b4c7a13f5a103002": "Secure the distribution records",
    "69ea1003b4c7a13f5a103003": "Transfer the support data",

    "69ea1004b4c7a13f5a001004 name": "Closed Circuits",
    "69ea1004b4c7a13f5a001004 description": "Mechanic doesn’t tolerate drift.\n\nHis people move parts because they know exactly where those parts are expected to be.\n\nThat kind of precision makes the whole system narrow.\n\nNarrow systems are harder to hide inside.\n\nBring me the records that define how his work travels.\n\nI want the architecture, not the rumor.",
    "69ea1004b4c7a13f5a001004 startedMessageText": "Get the records. Precision always leaves a line to follow.",
    "69ea1004b4c7a13f5a001004 successMessageText": "Tight. Deliberate. Exactly the kind of structure I was looking for.",
    "69ea1004b4c7a13f5a001004 completePlayerMessage": "Technical records secured and transferred.",
    "69ea1004b4c7a13f5a001004 declinePlayerMessage": "",
    "69ea1004b4c7a13f5a001004 failMessageText": "An incomplete map of control is worse than none at all.",
    "69ea1004b4c7a13f5a001004 note": "Locate and extract technical records to define controlled movement channels.",

    "69ea1004b4c7a13f5a104001": "Locate Mechanic’s technical records in the Factory lower office",
    "69ea1004b4c7a13f5a104002": "Secure the technical records",
    "69ea1004b4c7a13f5a104003": "Transfer the technical data",

    "69ea1005b4c7a13f5a001005 name": "Clean Channels",
    "69ea1005b4c7a13f5a001005 description": "Anything that comes from outside gets treated like it arrived with legitimacy.\n\nThat assumption is useful to the people making money from it.\n\nIt’s also careless.\n\nFind where his imports first touch the network and bring me proof of it.\n\nThe route tells me more than the goods ever will.",
    "69ea1005b4c7a13f5a001005 startedMessageText": "Find the entry point and keep the rest of the route undisturbed.",
    "69ea1005b4c7a13f5a001005 successMessageText": "Good. Once you know where it starts, the rest follows on its own.",
    "69ea1005b4c7a13f5a001005 completePlayerMessage": "Import records secured and transferred.",
    "69ea1005b4c7a13f5a001005 declinePlayerMessage": "",
    "69ea1005b4c7a13f5a001005 failMessageText": "No clean entry point means no reliable chain behind it.",
    "69ea1005b4c7a13f5a001005 note": "Locate and extract import records to identify external entry routes.",

    "69ea1005b4c7a13f5a105001": "Locate Peacekeeper’s import records at the Shoreline pier",
    "69ea1005b4c7a13f5a105002": "Secure the import records",
    "69ea1005b4c7a13f5a105003": "Transfer the import data",

    "69ea1006b4c7a13f5a001006 name": "Worn Paths",
    "69ea1006b4c7a13f5a001006 description": "Movement doesn’t need to look valuable to matter.\n\nSometimes the widest network is built from things nobody respects enough to watch.\n\nThat’s why it works.\n\nBring me the records showing how those goods spread through the city.\n\nCoverage matters more than glamour.",
    "69ea1006b4c7a13f5a001006 startedMessageText": "Follow the records where the movement broadens out.",
    "69ea1006b4c7a13f5a001006 successMessageText": "Wide reach. Quiet traffic. More influence than he probably intended.",
    "69ea1006b4c7a13f5a001006 completePlayerMessage": "Distribution records secured and transferred.",
    "69ea1006b4c7a13f5a001006 declinePlayerMessage": "",
    "69ea1006b4c7a13f5a001006 failMessageText": "If the spread isn’t clear, the network still has places to hide.",
    "69ea1006b4c7a13f5a001006 note": "Locate and extract distribution records to map broad civilian movement.",

    "69ea1006b4c7a13f5a106001": "Locate Ragman’s distribution records in the Goshan shipping area on Interchange",
    "69ea1006b4c7a13f5a106002": "Secure the distribution records",
    "69ea1006b4c7a13f5a106003": "Transfer the distribution data",

    "69ea1007b4c7a13f5a001007 name": "Unmarked Trails",
    "69ea1007b4c7a13f5a001007 description": "Jaeger doesn’t rely on formal systems.\n\nThat doesn’t mean he moves without leaving shape behind.\n\nSupplies still travel. Paths still form. Habits still appear.\n\nFind whatever he left that shows how those off-grid routes develop.\n\nIf it exists, I can read it.",
    "69ea1007b4c7a13f5a001007 startedMessageText": "Track the notes down. Irregular doesn’t mean invisible.",
    "69ea1007b4c7a13f5a001007 successMessageText": "There it is. Even disorder settles into pattern eventually.",
    "69ea1007b4c7a13f5a001007 completePlayerMessage": "Field notes secured and transferred.",
    "69ea1007b4c7a13f5a001007 declinePlayerMessage": "",
    "69ea1007b4c7a13f5a001007 failMessageText": "Too many blind spots remain. That’s not useful to me.",
    "69ea1007b4c7a13f5a001007 note": "Locate and extract field notes to identify off-grid supply movement.",

    "69ea1007b4c7a13f5a107001": "Locate Jaeger’s supply notes at the Woods hunting camp",
    "69ea1007b4c7a13f5a107002": "Secure the supply notes",
    "69ea1007b4c7a13f5a107003": "Transfer the field data",

    // ACT 3 Infiltration

    "68498dcea603d454abc11356 name": "Echo Traps",
    "68498dcea603d454abc11356 description": "The city still talks.\n\nMost people just stopped listening properly.\n\nOld systems, dead infrastructure, forgotten channels — they all keep carrying pieces of useful traffic.\n\nThat changes now.\n\nSet the devices at points where information actually passes through and leave them there without drawing attention.\n\nOnce they’re active, I won’t need permission to hear what matters.",
    "68498dcea603d454abc11356 startedMessageText": "Place the devices carefully. No one should know they’re there.",
    "68498dcea603d454abc11356 successMessageText": "Good. I’m hearing more than I was before.",
    "68498dcea603d454abc11356 completePlayerMessage": "Devices planted. No exposure.",
    "68498dcea603d454abc11356 declinePlayerMessage": "",
    "68498dcea603d454abc11356 failMessageText": "That placement carried too much risk. Attention ruins the whole point.",
    "68498dcea603d454abc11356 note": "Place listening devices to intercept live communication traffic unnoticed.",

    "5eca9553f3a992fe7186ffe8": "Place a listening device inside the Customs office at Big Red",
    "15981ab8ec8aa954a205a4fc": "Place a listening device inside the new gas station office",
    "603e1e94b031722bf688626d": "Place a listening device inside the crackhouse office",
    "500ee99122dbc04cf35d873e": "Extract without exposing the placements",

    "69d81cd30ffb6f16a7c38e69 name": "Family Debts",
    "69d81cd30ffb6f16a7c38e69 description": "Before people started pretending everything in Tarkov ran on contracts, it ran on trust and placement.\n\nSomething left where it was supposed to be. Someone else arrives later and collects it.\n\nNo chatter. No correction.\n\nThat method never disappeared.\n\nIt just changed owners.\n\nThere’s a package waiting inside the fortress.\n\nTake it cleanly and leave the wider system undisturbed.\n\nIf nothing reacts, then expectation held even after we touched it.",
    "69d81cd30ffb6f16a7c38e69 startedMessageText": "Secure the package and leave the handoff looking untouched.",
    "69d81cd30ffb6f16a7c38e69 successMessageText": "Good. No visible reaction. That means the system absorbed it.",
    "69d81cd30ffb6f16a7c38e69 completePlayerMessage": "Package taken. No response followed.",
    "69d81cd30ffb6f16a7c38e69 declinePlayerMessage": "",
    "69d81cd30ffb6f16a7c38e69 failMessageText": "If they noticed the absence, then we learned less than we should have.",
    "69d81cd30ffb6f16a7c38e69 note": "Intercept a dead-drop package without disturbing the surrounding system.",

    "64bfa8d68cfc2ae1e2da5d42": "Eliminate Scavs to secure the Customs fortress drop site",
    "c2ed95c197979810dd2af094": "Secure the staged package from the fortress",
    "e8f66e0884d4751636f4ab6f": "Extract with the package without drawing attention",

    "69d81ce56cd2ce07a50d79d2 name": "Silent Couriers",
    "69d81ce56cd2ce07a50d79d2 description": "Routes aren’t really about moving objects.\n\nThey move assumptions.\n\nSomething gets staged. Someone expects it to be there. The handoff works because nobody has reason to question it.\n\nThat’s what I want tested.\n\nTake the sealed packages from active points and do it without disturbing the route around them.\n\nIf the system keeps breathing normally after that, then we’re already further inside than they know.",
    "69d81ce56cd2ce07a50d79d2 startedMessageText": "Take the packages cleanly. Let the routes keep breathing.",
    "69d81ce56cd2ce07a50d79d2 successMessageText": "Good. No visible correction. That tells me plenty.",
    "69d81ce56cd2ce07a50d79d2 completePlayerMessage": "Packages intercepted. The routes stayed quiet.",
    "69d81ce56cd2ce07a50d79d2 declinePlayerMessage": "",
    "69d81ce56cd2ce07a50d79d2 failMessageText": "The route shifted around you. That means the system felt the interruption.",
    "69d81ce56cd2ce07a50d79d2 note": "Intercept active route packages without forcing route correction.",

    "b6930a22afb94f56ab426741": "Secure the sealed package at the Woods sawmill",
    "68dc5482cd37d4f04dd75455": "Secure the sealed package in Customs warehouse 6",
    "7a458d853e490f3cb3ef42cb": "Secure the sealed package at the Interchange village stage",
    "6f538c7593e38a7f916e18f0": "Extract without exposing the interceptions",

    // ACT 4 Control

    "69d81cf3caf46e08a1002df2 name": "Old Accounts",
    "69d81cf3caf46e08a1002df2 description": "Every network eventually writes itself down.\n\nNot because it wants to, but because scale demands memory.\n\nNumbers, timing, payment, placement — all of it ends up somewhere physical if the people behind it trust permanence more than secrecy.\n\nOne of them did.\n\nGet the ledger intact.\n\nNo missing pages. No damage.\n\nIf the records are whole, then so is the system behind them.",
    "69d81cf3caf46e08a1002df2 startedMessageText": "Take the ledger whole. Damage makes it worthless to me.",
    "69d81cf3caf46e08a1002df2 successMessageText": "Good. This is the spine they built around.",
    "69d81cf3caf46e08a1002df2 completePlayerMessage": "Ledger secured intact.",
    "69d81cf3caf46e08a1002df2 declinePlayerMessage": "",
    "69d81cf3caf46e08a1002df2 failMessageText": "Compromised records mean compromised leverage.",
    "69d81cf3caf46e08a1002df2 note": "Secure intact financial records to make the larger system readable.",

    "80d9fe503cbd9866053f7eb2": "Locate the financial ledger behind KIBA on Interchange",
    "b961749deb014e3407999cbb": "Secure the financial ledger intact",
    "b961749deb014e3407999cbc": "Transfer the ledger without damage",

    "69d81cfdc17c3b97d031ff08 name": "The Shipment",
    "69d81cfdc17c3b97d031ff08 description": "Cargo is just weight.\n\nWhat matters is who knows where that weight is supposed to be and when.\n\nThat’s control.\n\nThere’s a transfer on Lighthouse still moving because everyone involved trusts the record behind it.\n\nTake the manifest and leave the shipment itself alone.\n\nIf the route keeps moving afterward, then the cargo was never the valuable part.\n\nThe information was.",
    "69d81cfdc17c3b97d031ff08 startedMessageText": "Take the manifest. Leave the transfer untouched.",
    "69d81cfdc17c3b97d031ff08 successMessageText": "Good. The cargo kept moving, but the control behind it didn’t.",
    "69d81cfdc17c3b97d031ff08 completePlayerMessage": "Manifest secured. Route stayed intact.",
    "69d81cfdc17c3b97d031ff08 declinePlayerMessage": "",
    "69d81cfdc17c3b97d031ff08 failMessageText": "If movement changed, then we gave away the advantage.",
    "69d81cfdc17c3b97d031ff08 note": "Secure the shipment manifest to take control without stopping the route.",

    "7003c9afb0e78a6668ec37e3": "Locate the shipment manifest in the Lighthouse trainyard warehouse",
    "39e306f06c18c3a46d2036f6": "Secure the manifest without disrupting the transfer",
    "09505e3d24603629cddb37ce": "Extract with the manifest without exposure",

    // ACT 4.5 Convergence

    "69ea1999c0nverg3nc300001 name": "Convergence",
    "69ea1999c0nverg3nc300001 description": "I’ve gone back through everything you brought me.\n\nNot one piece at a time.\n\nAs a whole.\n\nSkier’s routes. Prapor’s cycles. Therapist’s flow. Mechanic’s precision. Peacekeeper’s entry points. Ragman’s spread. Jaeger’s field movement.\n\nSeparate on the surface.\n\nConnected underneath.\n\nThat was deliberate.\n\nThe devices confirmed the network listens and adjusts. The dead-drops proved expectation can survive interference. The sealed packages showed those routes can be touched without immediate correction. The ledger explained the structure beneath it. The manifest proved control belongs to whoever owns the record.\n\nThat should have been enough.\n\nIt wasn’t.\n\nNow I want to know whether this thing can absorb us completely or whether it’s already pushing back.\n\nMark the train cars moving cargo through the active network.\n\nNot to track them.\n\nTo test whether being touched changes anything at all.\n\nIf nothing shifts, we’re inside it.\n\nIf it does, then we triggered something bigger than control.",
    "69ea1999c0nverg3nc300001 startedMessageText": "Mark the routes and keep your footprint light.",
    "69ea1999c0nverg3nc300001 successMessageText": "…Interesting. Either the system accepted it, or it hid the reaction well enough to matter.",
    "69ea1999c0nverg3nc300001 completePlayerMessage": "Routes marked. No obvious disruption followed.",
    "69ea1999c0nverg3nc300001 declinePlayerMessage": "",
    "69ea1999c0nverg3nc300001 failMessageText": "Something moved when it shouldn’t have. That changes what this means.",
    "69ea1999c0nverg3nc300001 note": "Mark active transport routes to test how the network responds to interference.",

    "69ea1999c0nverg3nc310001": "Mark the cargo train car at the Customs train depot",
    "69ea1999c0nverg3nc310002": "Mark the military supply train car on Reserve",
    "69ea1999c0nverg3nc310003": "Mark the shipping train car at the Lighthouse trainyard",
    "69ea1999c0nverg3nc310004": "Avoid unnecessary combat while marking the routes",
    "69ea1999c0nverg3nc310005": "Extract after confirming no disruption to the network",

    // ACT 5 Fracture
    // Crossed Wires Good Questline

    "69d81d08b08a9cf2a881f70e name": "Crossed Wires",
    "69d81d08b08a9cf2a881f70e description": "I watched the marked routes.\n\nNothing meaningful changed.\n\nNo rerouting. No delays. No compensation.\n\nThe cargo moved as if the network had already decided we belonged there.\n\nThat matters.\n\nIt means the structure accepted the pressure without rejecting it.\n\nBut acceptance adds weight.\n\nTwo points are carrying more than they were built for now.\n\nFactory and Reserve.\n\nReinforce them quietly.\n\nIf they hold, then what we built becomes permanent instead of temporary.",
    "69d81d08b08a9cf2a881f70e startedMessageText": "Reinforce the weak points and keep the system calm.",
    "69d81d08b08a9cf2a881f70e successMessageText": "Good. No buckling. No correction. It held.",
    "69d81d08b08a9cf2a881f70e completePlayerMessage": "Nodes stabilized. The system held steady.",
    "69d81d08b08a9cf2a881f70e declinePlayerMessage": "",
    "69d81d08b08a9cf2a881f70e failMessageText": "If the load slipped there, then control isn’t settled yet.",
    "69d81d08b08a9cf2a881f70e note": "Stabilize critical network nodes to lock in system control.",

    "603207d9f2bef8d2219dd0ca": "Stabilize the Factory control node using a toolkit",
    "69e35ba684eda35b8d279376": "Stabilize the Reserve command node using a toolkit",
    "57f8473740b35132ec9a0012": "Extract without triggering a system response",

    // Crossed Wires Bad Questline

    "69d81d08b08a9cf2a881f70f name": "Crossed Wires",
    "69d81d08b08a9cf2a881f70f description": "I watched the marked routes.\n\nThey changed.\n\nNot enough for most people to notice, but enough to matter.\n\nTiming drifted. Cargo stalled where it shouldn’t have. Small corrections appeared across lines that should have ignored each other.\n\nThat isn’t random.\n\nThat’s reaction.\n\nNow I need to know whether the network is unstable by nature or whether it’s unstable because of you.\n\nIntroduce controlled faults into the same structure.\n\nKeep them precise.\n\nIf the response repeats, then the pattern tells me where the real problem is.",
    "69d81d08b08a9cf2a881f70f startedMessageText": "Introduce the fault and let the system show its hand.",
    "69d81d08b08a9cf2a881f70f successMessageText": "There. Same behavior, same correction. That narrows things considerably.",
    "69d81d08b08a9cf2a881f70f completePlayerMessage": "Fault introduced. Response confirmed.",
    "69d81d08b08a9cf2a881f70f declinePlayerMessage": "",
    "69d81d08b08a9cf2a881f70f failMessageText": "No matching reaction means the read is still incomplete.",
    "69d81d08b08a9cf2a881f70f note": "Corrupt key nodes to measure and confirm system instability.",

    "69e35e5e06b9d69fd0ec0ed4": "Corrupt the Factory control node using a toolkit",
    "69e35e6154de368f5a3d5206": "Corrupt the Reserve command node using a toolkit",
    "57f8473740b35132ec9a0013": "Extract after confirming the system reacts",

    // ACT 6 Endings

    "69d81d10f141ade1c2f23cbd name": "Blood Oath",
    "69d81d10f141ade1c2f23cbd description": "You’ve gone too far inside this structure to stay undefined.\n\nThat kind of access needs a direction.\n\nNow you choose it.\n\nAct openly in my interest and make sure anyone watching understands what changed.\n\nAfter this, there’s no distance between you and the system.\n\nYou’ll be part of it in a way nobody can mistake.",
    "69d81d10f141ade1c2f23cbd startedMessageText": "Use what I gave you. Make the alignment obvious.",
    "69d81d10f141ade1c2f23cbd successMessageText": "Good. Clear action. No ambiguity left in it.",
    "69d81d10f141ade1c2f23cbd completePlayerMessage": "Targets eliminated. Position made clear.",
    "69d81d10f141ade1c2f23cbd declinePlayerMessage": "",
    "69d81d10f141ade1c2f23cbd failMessageText": "Hesitation weakens loyalty before anyone even tests it.",
    "69d81d10f141ade1c2f23cbd note": "Eliminate targets with Tony’s equipment to demonstrate open loyalty.",

    "ed9c12d309e06158faa7f816": "Eliminate PMCs using the provided equipment",

    "69d81d2211b64abb3f86ee12 name": "Clean House",
    "69d81d2211b64abb3f86ee12 description": "Once control settles in, resistance changes shape.\n\nIt stops looking like opposition and starts looking like hesitation inside the structure itself.\n\nThat’s more dangerous.\n\nThese people aren’t enemies because they’re strong.\n\nThey’re enemies because they create drag.\n\nRemove them without shaking the wider network.\n\nIf nothing ripples outward, then authority is real.",
    "69d81d2211b64abb3f86ee12 startedMessageText": "Remove the liabilities and keep the system steady.",
    "69d81d2211b64abb3f86ee12 successMessageText": "Good. The instability ended where it started.",
    "69d81d2211b64abb3f86ee12 completePlayerMessage": "Liabilities removed. Network remained stable.",
    "69d81d2211b64abb3f86ee12 declinePlayerMessage": "",
    "69d81d2211b64abb3f86ee12 failMessageText": "Leave instability in place and it starts teaching the system bad habits.",
    "69d81d2211b64abb3f86ee12 note": "Eliminate internal instability without disturbing the wider network.",

    "1e9026da7e4c46af8c992148": "Eliminate compromised operatives on Streets without disrupting the system",

    "69d81d2e489341684c932b76 name": "The New Boss",
    "69d81d2e489341684c932b76 description": "At this point, influence isn’t enough.\n\nThe routes answer correctly. The timing holds. The weak parts have been removed.\n\nNow the system needs a center.\n\nSecure the control point and make it undeniable.\n\nWhen this is finished, you won’t just work inside the structure.\n\nYou’ll be part of what defines it.\n\nNothing local moves without passing through your authority first.",
    "69d81d2e489341684c932b76 startedMessageText": "Take the control point and make the authority stick.",
    "69d81d2e489341684c932b76 successMessageText": "Good. That’s not influence anymore. That’s rule.",
    "69d81d2e489341684c932b76 completePlayerMessage": "Control point secured. Authority established.",
    "69d81d2e489341684c932b76 declinePlayerMessage": "",
    "69d81d2e489341684c932b76 failMessageText": "If the point doesn’t hold, then the rest stays negotiable.",
    "69d81d2e489341684c932b76 note": "Secure the control point to establish permanent authority over the network.",

    "fd122acd465f88fd577be25f": "Eliminate all resistance at the control point",
    "05ebbaa447ffa8affb05b1f1": "Extract after securing control",

    // 1️⃣ COMMITMENT — MIRROR OF BLOOD OATH (Factory)

    "69d81d3d82a2da467ea1fdba name": "Loose Ends",
    "69d81d3d82a2da467ea1fdba description": "You’ve gone too far inside this structure to stay undefined.\n\nAccess like that always resolves one way or another.\n\nNow it does.\n\nThere’s a control point in Factory still answering to him.\n\nFor now.\n\nClear the area, place the tracker, and leave before anyone understands what changed.\n\nAfter this, the system won’t be closed anymore.\n\nIt will be exposed.\n\nAnd once something like this is exposed… it doesn’t stay intact.",
    "69d81d3d82a2da467ea1fdba startedMessageText": "Clear the node. Plant the tracker. Leave no trace.",
    "69d81d3d82a2da467ea1fdba successMessageText": "Good. The opening is there, and no one inside it has noticed yet.",
    "69d81d3d82a2da467ea1fdba completePlayerMessage": "Area cleared. Tracker planted. Access opened.",
    "69d81d3d82a2da467ea1fdba declinePlayerMessage": "",
    "69d81d3d82a2da467ea1fdba failMessageText": "If they detect the breach now, the rest won’t unfold the way it should.",
    "69d81d3d82a2da467ea1fdba note": "Clear the Factory control node and plant a tracker to expose the system.",

    "a5ab7af2349a3ed39a36cb67": "Plant the tracker inside the Factory control office",
    "04866af5282f607ef18a9a5c": "Extract without detection",

    // 2️⃣ DESTABILIZATION — MIRROR OF CLEAN HOUSE (Factory + Reserve)

    "69d81d46670bc1df8b8c3ed1 name": "Collapse the Family",
    "69d81d46670bc1df8b8c3ed1 description": "Pressure changes how systems behave.\n\nAt first, it looks like resistance.\n\nThen it starts looking like fracture.\n\nThat’s where we are now.\n\nThe Factory node is open.\n\nReserve is still holding the structure together.\n\nThat’s where it breaks.\n\nExpose the information tied to both locations and remove anyone trying to contain the spread.\n\nIf the damage travels between them, the system stops acting like a system.\n\nIt starts acting like something failing.",
    "69d81d46670bc1df8b8c3ed1 startedMessageText": "Expose both nodes and stop containment before it spreads.",
    "69d81d46670bc1df8b8c3ed1 successMessageText": "Good. The reaction didn’t stay local. That’s what I needed to see.",
    "69d81d46670bc1df8b8c3ed1 completePlayerMessage": "Intel exposed. Containment failed. Instability spreading.",
    "69d81d46670bc1df8b8c3ed1 declinePlayerMessage": "",
    "69d81d46670bc1df8b8c3ed1 failMessageText": "If they contain it here, the structure still has discipline left.",
    "69d81d46670bc1df8b8c3ed1 note": "Expose operational intel at Factory and Reserve and prevent containment.",

    "89129bf73f1a1cd7195d810a": "Expose sensitive operational intel in the Factory control area",
    "5ecb271f100905c558efb754": "Expose sensitive operational intel in the Reserve bunker command area",
    "81efd48874515f97e6765765": "Eliminate operatives attempting to contain the spread at both locations",
    "81efd48874515f97e6765766": "Extract after the instability spreads",

    // 3️⃣ FINAL STATE — MIRROR OF THE NEW BOSS (Streets)

    "69d81d50db716124768a70a0 name": "Fall of the Fixer",
    "69d81d50db716124768a70a0 description": "At this point, instability isn’t enough.\n\nThe routes are slipping. Timing is failing. The structure is already under pressure.\n\nBut it still has a center.\n\nThat’s the problem.\n\nEverything still traces back to a point that keeps it functioning.\n\nRemove it.\n\nGo to Streets. Find what’s left holding the network together and eliminate it.\n\nWhen this is done, nothing will move the way it used to.\n\nNot because it changed.\n\nBecause there’s nothing left to control it.",
    "69d81d50db716124768a70a0 startedMessageText": "Remove what’s left of the system’s control.",
    "69d81d50db716124768a70a0 successMessageText": "…Yes. That’s not instability anymore. That’s removal.",
    "69d81d50db716124768a70a0 completePlayerMessage": "Operators eliminated. System control collapsed.",
    "69d81d50db716124768a70a0 declinePlayerMessage": "",
    "69d81d50db716124768a70a0 failMessageText": "If anything still answers correctly, then the structure isn’t gone yet.",
    "69d81d50db716124768a70a0 note": "Eliminate remaining operators on Streets to remove the system’s control center.",

    "96ff16c0c85a8fff88512685": "Eliminate all remaining network operators at the Streets control point (Lexos)",
    "05ebbaa447ffa8affb05b1f2": "Extract after confirming system collapse",

